// Four equal bars, 5:3, from the designer's image (1188 by 713 pixels).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Aroace spectrum flag"
  designer "theflagarchive (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2020-08-08"
  series "aroace-spectrum-flag"
  version "four-stripe-2020"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/2021/https://theflagarchive.tumblr.com/post/625841657548587008/aroace-spectrum-flag-a-flag-for-anybody-who-has-a"
  note "Designer's own post on the Tumblr blog Flag Archive (theflagarchive), read from a 2021 Wayback snapshot of the address above; the page's metadata dates it 2020-08-08 (01:11 in UTC-4, so 7 August in some time zones). It calls it 'a flag for anybody who has a lack of romantic and sexual attraction, or differing experiences with romantic and sexual attraction to where they would consider themselves aspec'."
  note "The post has two images, the flag and the flag with each bar's meaning written on it: green, lack of or different experiences with romantic attraction; pale cyan, diversity in experiences and attraction; purple, lack of or different experiences with sexual attraction; dark blue, the community, solidarity and history. The colors were read from the plain image (1188 by 713 PNG, fetched from Tumblr's media server): #79c49b, #eafdfb, #635a9f, #11263e. The bars are equal, and the proportion 5:3 is the image's, 1188:713."
  note "This is a different flag from the aroace flag (aroace-flag) and the a-spec flag. Other designs have also been called aroace-spec or ay-spec flags; a ten-stripe one is aroace-spectrum-striped in the same series. The same post also appears on the author's other blog, potionflags (post 634633836865683456, November 2020), which the LGBTA Fandom wiki cited in a March 2021 Wayback snapshot."
}
palette {
  green "#79c49b"
  pale-cyan "#eafdfb"
  purple "#635a9f"
  dark-blue "#11263e"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars green pale-cyan purple dark-blue
